# Docker's build context has no concept of .gitignore -- COPY . . copies
# whatever is sitting in this directory on whichever machine runs the
# build, gitignored or not. Discovered for real while testing PR 21/22's
# Trivy gate: a local `docker build` baked in backend/.venv (a 223MB
# Windows-only dev virtualenv, unused and non-functional inside the Linux
# container) and it surfaced as two spurious CVE findings against packages
# the running app never actually imports. CI's own build starts from a
# fresh `actions/checkout` with none of this present, so production was
# never exposed -- but a build's output shouldn't depend on what happens
# to be lying around on whichever machine ran it.
.venv/
.coverage
.pytest_cache/
tmp/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
